From 2933087df413a3dfa21b13f2dda6aee8bb29b0c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:26:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: build the lean port with the compiler it pins

`lean/lean-toolchain` moved to v4.32.1 in 48392f5, for the reason that
commit gives: voxgig/struct's lean port and the sdkgen scaffold both pin
it, and four repositories vendored together as one checkpoint cannot be
compiled side by side on three different pins.

This file still fetched v4.15.0, so CI compiled 4.32.1 sources with a
compiler that predates the `String.Slice` changes 48392f5 was written
for. `make build-lean` has failed on every run since, on `main` as well
as on every branch, and it reads as a port failure rather than a
toolchain mismatch.

An agent session cannot write `.github/workflows/`, which is why the
port's bump landed without this. The comment now says the two must move
together, so the next bump has one place to look.

Verified: the v4.32.1 linux asset resolves at the URL this builds.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 9994820..36ec2c2 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -232,10 +232,17 @@ jobs:
       # The asset is `.tar.zst`; ubuntu-latest ships zstd, and the
       # explicit `--use-compress-program` says so rather than relying on
       # tar's suffix detection.
+      #
+      # THE VERSION HERE MUST MATCH `lean/lean-toolchain`, and an agent
+      # session cannot edit this file, so the two move in separate
+      # changes and the port's own bump lands first. When they drifted
+      # the job failed on `make build-lean` with the port's sources and
+      # the workflow's older compiler, which reads as a port failure and
+      # is not one.
       - if: matrix.port == 'lean'
         run: |
           curl -fsSL -o /tmp/lean.tar.zst \
-            https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/releases/download/v4.15.0/lean-4.15.0-linux.tar.zst
+            https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/releases/download/v4.32.1/lean-4.32.1-linux.tar.zst
           sudo mkdir -p /opt/lean
           sudo tar --use-compress-program=unzstd -xf /tmp/lean.tar.zst \
             -C /opt/lean --strip-components=1
-- 
2.43.0

